      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you think about indexing this array by the `enum boot_key` instead?\n\n```\nstruct boot_key_entry boot_key_list[] \u003d {\n    [BOOT_KEY_ESC] \u003d { KEYBOARD_COL_ESC, KEYBOARD_ROW_ESC },\n    ...\n```\n\nThen any boards that use `CONFIG_KEYBOARD_MULTIPLE`, can update the boot keys more intuitively.  For example, from [delbin keyboard customization](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/board/delbin/keyboard_customization.c;l\u003d141):\n\n```\nboot_key_list[BOOT_KEY_ESC].col \u003d KEYBOARD2_COL_ESC;\nboot_key_list[BOOT_KEY_ESC].row \u003d KEYBOARD2_ROW_ESC;\nboot_key_list[BOOT_KEY_DOWN_ARROW].col \u003d KEYBOARD2_COL_DOWN;\nboot_key_list[BOOT_KEY_DOWN_ARROW].row \u003d KEYBOARD2_ROW_DOWN;\nboot_key_list[BOOT_KEY_LEFT_SHIFT].col \u003d KEYBOARD2_COL_LEFT_SHIFT;\nboot_key_list[BOOT_KEY_LEFT_SHIFT].row \u003d KEYBOARD2_ROW_LEFT_SHIFT;\n```",
